!
! Line 51 is a full word, so THE COUNTER LEAVES THIS PAGE AT
! 217630.00.  printed p.153 line 4 prints "217630.00 *" against an
! SLC with no binary output, which is that value read back off
! IBM's own assembler on the next sheet.
!
! The banner on line 29 is 20 asterisks, "CHANGE MODE", 31
! asterisks, counted off the ink-run pitch (58.3 px at 600 dpi) and
! not off a glyph-by-glyph count; the two groups' end-to-end spans
! divide by that pitch to 19 and 30 intervals exactly.  The ";" on
! lines 32 and 33 is STRAP's statement separator, which this drum
! prints as a doubled dagger-like glyph; printed p.136 and printed
! p.127 establish the semicolon double-statement card, and lines
! 25/26 and 46/47 here ARE such cards (see the serial column), but
! the separator itself is inside a COMMENT card here and no check
! can see it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THESE CHECKS DO AND DO NOT ESTABLISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All forty-two emitting rows are declared, and all five of the
! page's own labels.  Nothing that emits a bit on this page is left
! unchecked.
!
! THE REAL CHECKS OF THIS PAGE'S OWN COUNTING are the three rows
! whose operand is a label defined HERE, all three forward:
!   line 37  BAE,K K MODE       -> 217624.76, and K K MODE is line 48
!   line 38  LV,1,K M CODE-1.0  -> 217624.02, and K M CODE is line 49
!   line 39  SVA,1,K MODE C.32  -> 217622.43, and K MODE C is line 44
! Each resolves only if every intervening row's LENGTH is right,
! and line 39 reaches across the CNOP on line 41 that emits nothing
! -- so it is also the check that the CNOP is correctly silent.
! The six "$"-relative rows (lines 3, 7, 8, 14, 22, 42, 48) check
! the counter against itself one or two words at a time.
!
! >>> WHAT IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF WORD, MEASURED AND NOT
! ASSUMED. <<<  Each external was perturbed by ONE BIT and by
! THIRTY-TWO, with everything else fixed, and the forty-two rows
! re-rendered:
!   A ONE-BIT CHANGE SHOWS (so this page pins them to the bit):
!     S RD, S HS ECH, S LOC SU, S CH OP, S SEL, S C MODE, S ARCAD,
!     S CW, S DD, K G LOCR, K EOP R.
!   ONLY A THIRTY-TWO-BIT CHANGE SHOWS (so ".00"/".40" is read and
!   anything below bit 32 is a CONVENTION here):
!     S CU ARC, S MX ARC, S IO INS, K SUPP, M IOREJ, K C BUSY,
!     K ILEGL, K K LOC, Z STEVL, K G LOC, K SEOP T.
!   The second group is the LVI / plain-branch / branch-on-bit-A /
!   direct-index-address forms of docs/transcription_workflow.md's
!   "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 1.  NOTE that the DIRECT INDEX
!   address field behaves the same way: S CU ARC at 6.00 and at
!   6.01 render identically on lines 16 and 19.  Every one of the
!   eleven is nevertheless pinned by a card on another page, cited
!   under EXTERNALS.
!
! >>> S DD IS PINNED ONLY MOD 128. <<<  Line 10 writes its byte
! size as "9-S DD" and that field is seven bits, so the row
! establishes 9-S DD = 9 (mod 128) and nothing more --
! "L(BU,9)" and "L(BU,9-S DD)" render the same word.  S DD = 0
! exactly comes from printed p.108's defining card, a different
! page.  This is "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 4, in the same shape
! printed p.129 found it.
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS ASSERTED, NOT CHECKED. <<<  See THE JOINS.
!
! TAUTOLOGY AUDIT: none.  Every external is defined by a card on
! another printed page; no row below is checking a value this page
! itself supplied.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: none.
! Every printed statement on this page was handed to strap_asm in
! its printed form and every one was accepted, including the
! three-operand VFL forms with a negative offset
! ("L(BU,18),S ARCAD($10),-18"), the connective-for-test
! "CT0111(BU,9)", the symbolic byte size "9-S DD", the
! store-field "SF(BU,2)", the I/O "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0", the
! bare "CNOP" that emits nothing, the trailing-comma index words
! "XW,(8)57.," and the branch-on-bit-and-set-to-one "BZB1".  The
! only substitutions are the ones the deck format requires and
! that the page itself licenses: names written closed up (the page
! prints "S HS ECH" and "SHSECH" for the same symbol, and
! "M IOREJ" and "M IO REJ"), and the SLC the page does not print.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   ZDISK1   217577.00
!SYM   KMODE    217615.00
!SYM   KMODEC   217622.00
!SYM   KKMODE   217624.40
!SYM   KMCODE   217625.00
!CHECK 217573.00 | 000000.71 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 1 CM1111(BU,1),S RD($11) -- the first row on the page, which the survey lost; byte 8B is i1 = $11 = 11 decimal
!CHECK 217574.00 | 000000.51 04 | line 2 KVI,4,.32 -- .32 decimal immediate prints .40 octal, plus J=4's .10 and KVI's .01
!CHECK 217574.40 | 217576.32 C0 | line 3 BZXE,$+1.32 (same card as line 2) -- target 217576.00
!CHECK 217575.00 | 215001.01 80 001000.36 F0 | line 4 CM1111(BU,1),S HS ECH -- printed "CM1111" and "001000.36"; CM0000 would print 001000.00
!CHECK 217576.00 | 216242.03 01 | line 5 LVI,1,K SUPP -- the .03 is LVI's operation bits, not address bits
!CHECK 217576.40 | 221261.10 00 | line 6 B,M IOREJ (same card as line 5)
!CHECK 217577.00 | 215001.21 80 217601.34 02 | line 7 ZDISK1 BB,SLOCSU,$+2.0 -- printed p.151 and p.153 both branch here, which pins this page's origin
!CHECK 217600.00 | 215001.01 80 217602.34 00 | line 8 BZB,SHSECH,$+2.0 -- printed "SHSECH" closed up, against line 4's "S HS ECH"; byte 00 vs line 7's 02 is the BZB/BB cond bit
!CHECK 217601.00 | 000000.32 8A 221065.34 06 | line 9 BBZ,SCHOP($10),KCBUSY -- byte 06 checks the "and zero" modifier; BB would print 02
!CHECK 217602.00 | 000003.34 8D 011067.20 50 | line 10 L(BU,9-S DD),S CW.28($13),-18 -- the leading 011 of the second half word is the byte size 9 octal, so S DD is pinned mod 128 only
!CHECK 217603.00 | 000010.20 30 | line 11 LV,8,$L -- $L is word 0o10, J=8 prints .20
!CHECK 217603.40 | 000003.45 8D 011062.57 70 | line 12 CT0111(BU,9),S CW+.37($13),-27 -- printed "CTO111"; the four connective digits are checked by .57 (CT0000 prints .41, CT1111 .77)
!CHECK 217604.40 | 217605.74 C0 | line 14 BZRZ,$+1.0 -- printed byte really is C0 and not 00 (1800 dpi); BRZ prints C2
!CHECK 217605.00 | 000001.21 0D | line 15 V-I,8,1.0 -SUBTRACT 1 FOR FULL ARC REQUEST
!CHECK 217605.40 | 000006.20 BD | line 16 V+,8,S CU ARC($13) -- byte D is i = $13 = 13 decimal
!CHECK 217606.00 | 000005.60 9D | line 17 KV,8,S MX ARC($13) -- .60 is S MX ARC's own .40 plus J=8's .20 (this LOCATION carries the unexplained second asterisk)
!CHECK 217606.40 | 220064.33 42 | line 18 BXH,K ILEGL -- BXL would print .32, BXE .32 with byte C2
!CHECK 217607.00 | 000006.00 3D | line 19 LV,0,S CU ARC($13) -- J=0, so this row prints S CU ARC bare, against line 16's J=8
!CHECK 217607.40 | 000000.40 8A 022067.20 50 | line 20 L(BU,18),S ARCAD($10),-18 -- 022 is the byte size 18 decimal
!CHECK 217610.40 | 000010.00 90 | line 21 KV,0,$L -TEST IF LOC NEEDED
!CHECK 217611.00 | 217612.72 C2 | line 22 BXE,$+1.32 -- target 217612.40, and the .40 shows as bit 18 of the address field inside the printed .72
!CHECK 217611.40 | 215001.21 80 220065.74 0C | line 23 BZB1,SLOCSU,KKLOC -- printed "CC"; the first glyph is a damaged 0 and the second a real C, and the pair is what spells BZB1 (BZB prints 00, BZBZ 04, BZBN 08, BB1 0E)
!CHECK 217612.40 | 000000.47 8B 221144.74 04 | line 24 BZBZ,S SEL($11),Z STEVL -- the .74 and line 27's .50 are the same Z STEVL read two ways
!CHECK 217613.40 | 220105.40 80 | line 25 SIC,K G LOCR -- SIC prints the bare 24-bit address, so this row pins K G LOCR to the bit
!CHECK 217614.00 | 220100.50 00 | line 26 B,K G LOC (same card as line 25; the SIC/branch pair is complete on this page)
!CHECK 217614.40 | 221144.50 00 | line 27 B,Z STEVL -- .50 is Z STEVL's .40 plus B's .10
!CHECK 217615.00 | 000010.03 30 | line 35 K MODE SV,1,$L -- three other pages print "B,K MODE" against 217615.10, which pins this label from outside
!CHECK 217615.40 | 000000.62 8A 002067.23 10 | line 36 KF(BU,2),S C MODE($10),-18 -- K would print .21, KFE byte 30, KR .21/50
!CHECK 217616.40 | 217624.76 C2 | line 37 BAE,K K MODE -- forward reference to line 48, a real check of this page's counting
!CHECK 217617.00 | 217624.02 31 | line 38 LV,1,K M CODE-1.0($1) -- forward reference to line 49 minus one word
!CHECK 217617.40 | 217622.43 D0 | line 39 SVA,1,K MODE C.32 -- forward reference to line 44 plus 32 bits (prints .40) plus SVA's J=1 and .01; it reaches across the silent CNOP on line 41
!CHECK 217620.00 | 000000.62 8A 002067.12 F0 | line 40 SF(BU,2),S C MODE($10),-18 -- ST would print 002067.20 D0
!CHECK 217621.00 | 217622.00 10 | line 42 LX,0,$+1.
!CHECK 217621.40 | 000004.01 1C | line 43 SX,0,S IO INS($12) (same card as line 42) -- byte C is i = $12 = 12 decimal (this LOCATION carries the unexplained second asterisk)
!CHECK 217622.00 | 000000.00 8E 000000.15 00 | line 44 K MODE C CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),0.0 -- the .15 checks CTL against RD(SEOP) .11, W(SEOP) .13, LOC(SEOP) .17 and plain CTL .05; the 8E checks the index $14
!CHECK 217623.00 | 221350.43 01 | line 45 LVI,1,K SEOP T -- the .03 is LVI's operation bits; the .40 is K SEOP T's half word
!CHECK 217623.40 | 221354.40 80 | line 46 SIC,K EOP R -- a bare 24-bit address, so this row pins K EOP R to the bit
!CHECK 217624.00 | 221261.10 00 | line 47 B,M IO REJ (same card as line 46) -- printed "M IO REJ" against line 6's "M IOREJ"
!CHECK 217624.40 | 217624.50 00 | line 48 K K MODE B,$ -- the half-word branch the caller's SIC modifies; two other pages print "SIC,K K MODE" against 217624.40, which pins it to the bit from outside
